; ask-lane-router.fk — one ask door. A request arrives; this cell says which lane carries it,
; what that lane needs, and — when it cannot be carried — which single thing is missing.
;
; WHAT WAS MISSING, named plainly. The body has three local-native generation lanes running today:
; llama3.2:3b through form/native/metal/metal_ask.sh, DeepSeek-V4-Flash through ask_ds4.sh ->
; metal_dsv4_stack.sh, and the KAT/qwen35moe carving in metal_kat_block0.sh. The registry
; (form-stdlib/native-model-control-plane.fk) knows all of them as rows. Each has its own carrier.
; NOTHING routed a request BY the row — the caller picked a script, and picking a script is picking
; an answer before asking a question. receipts/2026-08-03-staleledger.md named this as unfinished
; work item 3. This cell is that item.
;
; WHY THIS IS NOT A SWITCH, which is the design and not a defence. A switch is configuration chosen
; before the body runs: FORM_DS4_BLOB named one file out of six, so the body was TOLD its world
; instead of looking at it. Every input to this cell is either something only the caller can know
; (which lane of work, which modality, how many steps, whether the answer may leave the machine) or
; something the HOST REPORTED after looking (today's date, whether a Metal device answered, which
; GGUFs model-discovery.fk found and what architecture each file's own header declares, which carrier
; scripts exist, which runtimes are on PATH). The choice is made while the body runs, from options
; the body found. switch-census.fk's ratchet is untouched by this cell: it adds no environment
; variable and no flag.
;
; THE THREE MEMBERS OF A ROUTE, and why a lane needs all three. This is the whole shape:
;
;   the ROW      the registry's witness statement — this lane exists, it is active, it was witnessed
;                on a day, its status is proven or observed or partial. AUTHORITY: may it answer.
;   the BLOB     a file on this host whose own header declares the architecture. GROUND: the bytes
;                are here. A row without a blob is a claim about somewhere else.
;   the CARRIER  a script this body wrote that carves that architecture. THE HAND: something can run
;                it. A row and a blob with no carrier is arithmetic nobody has hands for.
;
; A route is CARRIED when all three join and every derived need is met. Otherwise UNFINISHED, with
; the missing member named. There is no third verdict, and `alr-status?` does not carry one: Urs, 2026-08-03,
; "we support all silicon on all platforms, and if we find an issue that means unfinished work,
; nothing more" and "the only limit are the physical hardware and our imagination". A router that can
; say "unsupported" will eventually say it about work that was merely undone, so the word is absent
; from the type.
;
; WHY THE BINDINGS ARE A WITNESSED LIST AND NOT A DERIVATION. A registry row names a model
; ("DeepSeek-V4-Flash-REAP25-DSpark"); a GGUF on disk names a file
; (ds4flash-v5mx-reap25-type40-mxfp8lt-dspark-v1.gguf); the join between them is the ARCHITECTURE the
; file's header declares (deepseek4). I tried to derive that key from the model name by taking its
; leading token, and it is wrong on this very host: "DeepSeek-V4-..." lowercases to "deepseek", which
; matches the IQ2XXS chat blob and NOT the reap25 blob the lane actually runs. A derivation that is
; wrong on the first three cases is a guess wearing a function's name. So `alr-bindings` is a
; witnessed inventory in the same discipline as `nmcp-registry`: dated, correctable, and each row
; verifiable by reading the carrier that keys on that architecture.
;
; WHAT THIS CELL DOES NOT SPEAK FOR (aporon). It does not generate a token. It does not verify that
; the carrier it names will succeed — a present script and a present blob are necessary, never
; sufficient, and the carrier's own witnesses remain the proof that it computed anything. It does not
; adjudicate whether the blob it found is the SAME quantization the lane was witnessed against; three
; deepseek4 files sit on this host and this cell picks the first the host reported, which is a real
; seam named in the receipt rather than hidden behind a preference nobody wrote down.
;
; witnessed 2026-08-03 on M4 Max: six GGUFs under ~/models across three architectures —
; qwen35moe (41 layers), deepseek4 (43), llama (28) — read by model-discovery.fk from each file's
; own header, not from a list.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk, form-stdlib/native-model-control-plane.fk
;
; Proven by: form-stdlib/tests/ask-lane-router-band.fk

(do
    ; ---- the ask. Only the caller knows these; they are arguments, not knobs. ----------------
    ;   lane        the lane of work, matched against the registry row's own lane field
    ;   modality    text / audio / image / multimodal
    ;   steps       how far to walk. A cap, not a length.
    ;   floor       the least status this answer will accept: 3 proven, 2 observed, 1 partial
    ;   off-host?   may this question leave the machine. Consent, and nobody else can give it.
    (defn alr-ask (lane modality steps floor off-host)
        (list "alr-ask" lane modality steps floor off-host))
    (defn alr-ask? (a) (if (and (eq (len a) 6) (str_eq (nth a 0) "alr-ask")) 1 0))
    (defn alr-ask-lane (a) (nth a 1))
    (defn alr-ask-modality (a) (nth a 2))
    (defn alr-ask-steps (a) (nth a 3))
    (defn alr-ask-floor (a) (nth a 4))
    (defn alr-ask-off-host? (a) (nth a 5))

    ; ---- what the host reported, after looking. Observation, never configuration. ------------
    ; A blob is what model-discovery.fk returns for one file: its path, the architecture its OWN
    ; header declares, and the block count under that architecture's key.
    (defn alr-blob (path arch layers) (list "alr-blob" path arch layers))
    (defn alr-blob? (b) (if (and (eq (len b) 4) (str_eq (nth b 0) "alr-blob")) 1 0))
    (defn alr-blob-path (b) (nth b 1))
    (defn alr-blob-arch (b) (nth b 2))
    (defn alr-blob-layers (b) (nth b 3))

    ; A carrier is a script this body wrote, present on this host, that carves one architecture.
    (defn alr-carrier (path arch) (list "alr-carrier" path arch))
    (defn alr-carrier? (c) (if (and (eq (len c) 3) (str_eq (nth c 0) "alr-carrier")) 1 0))
    (defn alr-carrier-path (c) (nth c 1))
    (defn alr-carrier-arch (c) (nth c 2))

    (defn alr-host (day metal blobs carriers runtimes)
        (list "alr-host" day metal blobs carriers runtimes))
    (defn alr-host? (h) (if (and (eq (len h) 6) (str_eq (nth h 0) "alr-host")) 1 0))
    (defn alr-host-day (h) (nth h 1))
    (defn alr-host-metal? (h) (nth h 2))
    (defn alr-host-blobs (h) (nth h 3))
    (defn alr-host-carriers (h) (nth h 4))
    (defn alr-host-runtimes (h) (nth h 5))

    ; ---- the binding. Registry row id -> the architecture its recipe carves. -------------------
    ; Verifiable by reading the carrier: metal_first_token.sh keys on llama.block_count,
    ; metal_dsv4_stack.sh on deepseek4.block_count, kat-coder-layer-shape.fk on
    ; qwen35moe.full_attention_interval.
    ;
    ; AND WHY THE BIND CARRIES A KEY AS WELL AS AN ARCHITECTURE.  The first version joined on
    ; architecture alone, and the live run refuted it in one line: asked for general-text it returned
    ; CARRIED on /Users/ursmuff/models/form-llama-vital-ground-f16.gguf, because that file's header
    ; says `llama` and so does llama3.2:3b's.  They are not the same model — one is a form-trained
    ; checkpoint, the other the champion row's witnessed weights — and a router that hands a lane the
    ; wrong weights while reporting success is worse than one that says not yet.  An architecture says how
    ; a file is RUN; it does not say WHICH model it is.  So a bind also carries a key: a
    ; substring that needs to appear in the path.  An empty key means any file of that architecture will
    ; do, and it is a claim, not a default — say it only where it is true.
    (defn alr-bind (id arch key) (list "alr-bind" id arch key))
    (defn alr-bind-id (b) (nth b 1))
    (defn alr-bind-arch (b) (nth b 2))
    (defn alr-bind-key (b) (nth b 3))
    (defn alr-no-bind () (alr-bind "" "" ""))
    (defn alr-bindings ()
        (list
            ; the champion's weights are ollama's content-addressed blob; the registry row carries
            ; that same sha256 in its artifact field, so the key is checkable against the row.
            (alr-bind "base.llama32-3b-metal" "llama" "dde5aa3fc5ffc171")
            ; metal_dsv4_stack.sh's own default blob, and the row names REAP25 in its model field.
            (alr-bind "challenger.deepseek-ds4-metal" "deepseek4" "reap25")
            ; Form-native Qwen3.8 generate. The key is the filename token, not the arch:
            ; qwen35moe (KAT) is a different file and stays unbound until its own row vouches.
            (alr-bind "challenger.qwen38-27b-metal" "qwen35" "Qwen3.8")
            ; a component row that has never answered an ask.  Its key is empty because no file has
            ; been witnessed for it — when it answers, the key wants witnessing first.
            (alr-bind "llm.llama32-3b-gguf-partial" "llama" "")))

    ; ---- small honest tools --------------------------------------------------------------------
    (defn alr-present? (s) (if (gt (str_len s) 0) 1 0))
    (defn alr-name-in? (name xs)
        (if (eq (len xs) 0) 0
            (if (str_eq name (head xs)) 1 (alr-name-in? name (tail xs)))))
    (defn alr-has-metal? (runtime) (if (ge (str_find runtime "Metal" 0) 0) 1 0))

    (defn alr-bind-of (id binds)
        (if (eq (len binds) 0) (alr-no-bind)
            (if (str_eq (alr-bind-id (head binds)) id) (head binds)
                (alr-bind-of id (tail binds)))))
    (defn alr-arch-of (id binds) (alr-bind-arch (alr-bind-of id binds)))
    ; A blob answers a bind when its architecture matches AND its path carries the bind's key.  An
    ; empty key matches anything, which is why an empty key is a claim about the lane and not a
    ; shrug about the file.
    (defn alr-blob-answers? (blob bind)
        (if (str_eq (alr-blob-arch blob) (alr-bind-arch bind))
            (if (eq (str_len (alr-bind-key bind)) 0) 1
                (if (ge (str_find (alr-blob-path blob) (alr-bind-key bind) 0) 0) 1 0))
            0))
    (defn alr-blob-for (bind blobs)
        (if (eq (len blobs) 0) ""
            (if (eq (alr-blob-answers? (head blobs) bind) 1) (alr-blob-path (head blobs))
                (alr-blob-for bind (tail blobs)))))
    (defn alr-carrier-for (arch carriers)
        (if (eq (len carriers) 0) ""
            (if (str_eq (alr-carrier-arch (head carriers)) arch) (alr-carrier-path (head carriers))
                (alr-carrier-for arch (tail carriers)))))

    ; ---- status, ranked. A lane that is failing, pending or historical never answers. ----------
    ; trained-unpromoted sits with partial: the weights exist, the promotion did not happen, and a
    ; caller who asked for proven is not handed it quietly.
    (defn alr-status-rank (s)
        (if (str_eq s "proven") 3
            (if (str_eq s "observed") 2
                (if (str_eq s "partial") 1
                    (if (str_eq s "trained-unpromoted") 1 0)))))
    (defn alr-surface-rank (s)
        (if (str_eq s "native-recipe") 3
            (if (str_eq s "local-process") 2
                (if (str_eq s "remote-membrane") 1 0))))

    ; ---- what a lane needs, derived from its own surface and runtime -------------------------
    ; This is the answer to "what does that lane need", and it is read off the row rather than
    ; attached to it, so a row that changes surface changes its needs in the same edit.
    (defn alr-needs (row)
        (if (str_eq (nmcp-surface row) "native-recipe")
            (if (eq (alr-has-metal? (nmcp-runtime row)) 1)
                (list "fkwu" "metal-device" "model-blob" "carrier")
                (list "fkwu" "recipe-cell"))
            (if (str_eq (nmcp-surface row) "local-process")
                (list "host-process" (nmcp-runtime row))
                (list "network" "call-ledger" "off-host-consent"))))

    (defn alr-need-met? (need ask host bind)
        (if (str_eq need "fkwu") 1
            (if (str_eq need "recipe-cell") 1
                (if (str_eq need "metal-device") (alr-host-metal? host)
                    (if (str_eq need "model-blob")
                        (alr-present? (alr-blob-for bind (alr-host-blobs host)))
                        (if (str_eq need "carrier")
                            (alr-present?
                                (alr-carrier-for (alr-bind-arch bind) (alr-host-carriers host)))
                            (if (str_eq need "off-host-consent") (alr-ask-off-host? ask)
                                (alr-name-in? need (alr-host-runtimes host)))))))))
    (defn alr-first-unmet (needs ask host bind)
        (if (eq (len needs) 0) ""
            (if (eq (alr-need-met? (head needs) ask host bind) 1)
                (alr-first-unmet (tail needs) ask host bind)
                (head needs))))

    ; ---- admission. Each threshold stands alone, so a decline can name which one closed. -------
    (defn alr-lane-match? (row ask)
        (if (and (str_eq (nmcp-lane row) (alr-ask-lane ask))
                 (str_eq (nmcp-modality row) (alr-ask-modality ask))) 1 0))
    (defn alr-consent-ok? (row ask)
        (if (str_eq (nmcp-surface row) "remote-membrane")
            (if (eq (alr-ask-off-host? ask) 1) 1 0)
            1))
    (defn alr-admissible? (row ask host)
        (if (eq (alr-lane-match? row ask) 1)
            (if (eq (nmcp-active? row) 1)
                (if (eq (nmcp-fresh? row (alr-host-day host)) 1)
                    (if (ge (alr-status-rank (nmcp-status row)) (alr-ask-floor ask))
                        (alr-consent-ok? row ask)
                        0)
                    0)
                0)
            0))
    ; The first threshold that closed, in the same order the predicate walks them.  A decline that
    ; cannot say which membrane stopped it teaches the caller nothing.
    (defn alr-first-closed (row ask host)
        (if (eq (alr-lane-match? row ask) 0) "lane-or-modality"
            (if (eq (nmcp-active? row) 0) "row-not-active"
                (if (eq (nmcp-fresh? row (alr-host-day host)) 0) "witness-stale"
                    (if (lt (alr-status-rank (nmcp-status row)) (alr-ask-floor ask)) "status-below-floor"
                        (if (eq (alr-consent-ok? row ask) 0) "off-host-consent" "none"))))))

    ; ---- choosing. Status first, then how close to the metal, then witnessed priority. ---------
    ; Ties keep the incumbent, so the fold is stable and the same registry always answers the same.
    (defn alr-better (a b ask host)
        (if (eq (alr-admissible? a ask host) 0) b
            (if (eq (alr-admissible? b ask host) 0) a
                (if (gt (alr-status-rank (nmcp-status a)) (alr-status-rank (nmcp-status b))) a
                    (if (lt (alr-status-rank (nmcp-status a)) (alr-status-rank (nmcp-status b))) b
                        (if (gt (alr-surface-rank (nmcp-surface a)) (alr-surface-rank (nmcp-surface b))) a
                            (if (lt (alr-surface-rank (nmcp-surface a)) (alr-surface-rank (nmcp-surface b))) b
                                (if (gt (nmcp-priority a) (nmcp-priority b)) a b))))))))
    (defn alr-none-row ()
        (nmcp-model "none" "none" "none" "form-native" "component" "pending" "native-recipe"
            "none" "none" "none" "none" "none" "none" 0 0 0 0 "none" 0 1 0 0 0 0))
    (defn alr-choose-loop (rows best ask host)
        (if (eq (len rows) 0) best
            (alr-choose-loop (tail rows) (alr-better (head rows) best ask host) ask host)))
    (defn alr-choose (rows ask host)
        (alr-choose-loop rows (alr-none-row) ask host))

    ; The nearest miss: a row that wanted this lane but met a closed threshold.  Reported so an unfinished
    ; route points at work rather than at a wall.
    (defn alr-near-miss-loop (rows ask host)
        (if (eq (len rows) 0) (alr-none-row)
            (if (eq (alr-lane-match? (head rows) ask) 1) (head rows)
                (alr-near-miss-loop (tail rows) ask host))))

    ; ---- the route ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    (defn alr-route (status id arch carrier blob needs reason)
        (list "alr-route" status id arch carrier blob needs reason))
    (defn alr-route? (r) (if (and (eq (len r) 8) (str_eq (nth r 0) "alr-route")) 1 0))
    (defn alr-route-status (r) (nth r 1))
    (defn alr-route-id (r) (nth r 2))
    (defn alr-route-arch (r) (nth r 3))
    (defn alr-route-carrier (r) (nth r 4))
    (defn alr-route-blob (r) (nth r 5))
    (defn alr-route-needs (r) (nth r 6))
    (defn alr-route-reason (r) (nth r 7))
    ; Two verdicts, and the type carries no third.  See the header.
    (defn alr-status? (s) (if (str_eq s "carried") 1 (if (str_eq s "unfinished") 1 0)))
    (defn alr-carried? (r) (if (str_eq (alr-route-status r) "carried") 1 0))

    (defn alr-unfinished (id arch needs why)
        (alr-route "unfinished" id arch "" "" needs why))

    ; The route for one already-chosen row.  Split out so a caller who names a model by id gets the
    ; same walk as a caller who let the registry choose.
    (defn alr-route-row (row ask host binds)
        (if (eq (alr-admissible? row ask host) 1)
            (do
                (let bind (alr-bind-of (nmcp-id row) binds))
                (let arch (alr-bind-arch bind))
                (let needs (alr-needs row))
                (if (and (eq (alr-has-metal? (nmcp-runtime row)) 1) (eq (alr-present? arch) 0))
                    (alr-unfinished (nmcp-id row) "" needs
                        "no architecture is bound to this row; alr-bindings has not witnessed it")
                    (do
                        (let missing (alr-first-unmet needs ask host bind))
                        (if (eq (alr-present? missing) 1)
                            (alr-unfinished (nmcp-id row) arch needs
                                (str_concat "this lane needs " (str_concat missing
                                    ", and this host did not report it")))
                            (alr-route "carried" (nmcp-id row) arch
                                (alr-carrier-for arch (alr-host-carriers host))
                                (alr-blob-for bind (alr-host-blobs host))
                                needs
                                "row, blob and carrier all joined")))))
            (alr-unfinished (nmcp-id row) "" (list)
                (str_concat "this row cannot answer: " (alr-first-closed row ask host)))))

    ; The door.  A request and a host report go in; a route comes out, always one of two verdicts.
    (defn alr-ask-door (rows ask host binds)
        (do
            (let best (alr-choose rows ask host))
            (if (str_eq (nmcp-id best) "none")
                (do
                    (let near (alr-near-miss-loop rows ask host))
                    (if (str_eq (nmcp-id near) "none")
                        (alr-unfinished "none" "" (list)
                            (str_concat "no row in the registry carries the lane "
                                        (alr-ask-lane ask)))
                        (alr-unfinished (nmcp-id near) "" (list)
                            (str_concat "the nearest row cannot answer: "
                                        (alr-first-closed near ask host)))))
                (alr-route-row best ask host binds))))

    ; Naming a model directly: the caller chose an id, the registry still holds the authority.
    (defn alr-row-by-id (rows id)
        (if (eq (len rows) 0) (alr-none-row)
            (if (str_eq (nmcp-id (head rows)) id) (head rows)
                (alr-row-by-id (tail rows) id))))
    (defn alr-ask-door-by-id (rows ask host binds id)
        (do
            (let row (alr-row-by-id rows id))
            (if (str_eq (nmcp-id row) "none")
                (alr-unfinished id "" (list)
                    (str_concat "the registry holds no row with id " id)
                    )
                (alr-route-row row ask host binds))))

    ; ---- the mirror. What this host can run that no row has vouched for. ------------------------
    ; A blob whose architecture has a carrier and no bound registry row is capability the body has
    ; and has not said it has.  On 2026-08-03 that is qwen35moe: metal_kat_block0.sh carves it, the
    ; file is on disk, and the registry has no KAT row at all.  Surfacing it here is the difference
    ; between a router and a switchboard.
    (defn alr-vouched? (arch binds rows)
        (if (eq (len binds) 0) 0
            (if (str_eq (alr-bind-arch (head binds)) arch)
                (if (str_eq (nmcp-id (alr-row-by-id rows (alr-bind-id (head binds)))) "none")
                    (alr-vouched? arch (tail binds) rows)
                    1)
                (alr-vouched? arch (tail binds) rows))))
    (defn alr-unvouched-loop (blobs host binds rows acc)
        (if (eq (len blobs) 0) acc
            (do
                (let arch (alr-blob-arch (head blobs)))
                (alr-unvouched-loop (tail blobs) host binds rows
                    (if (and (eq (alr-present? (alr-carrier-for arch (alr-host-carriers host))) 1)
                             (and (eq (alr-vouched? arch binds rows) 0)
                                  (eq (alr-name-in? arch acc) 0)))
                        (cons arch acc) acc)))))
    (defn alr-unvouched (host binds rows)
        (alr-unvouched-loop (alr-host-blobs host) host binds rows (list)))

    ; ---- saying it out loud ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    (defn alr-say-needs (xs)
        (if (eq (len xs) 0) 0
            (do (print_str (str_concat "    needs   " (head xs))) (alr-say-needs (tail xs)))))
    (defn alr-say-route (r)
        (do
            (print_str (str_concat "— route: " (alr-route-status r)))
            (print_str (str_concat "    row     " (alr-route-id r)))
            (print_str (str_concat "    arch    " (alr-route-arch r)))
            (print_str (str_concat "    carrier " (alr-route-carrier r)))
            (print_str (str_concat "    blob    " (alr-route-blob r)))
            (alr-say-needs (alr-route-needs r))
            (print_str (str_concat "    because " (alr-route-reason r)))
            (alr-carried? r)))

    0)
